1
00:00:01,430 --> 00:00:06,230
<i>Spring break is over and we've 
started our second year of high school.</i>

2
00:00:12,280 --> 00:00:17,490
You're in Class 4, huh?
I guess we're gonna be apart again.

3
00:00:17,490 --> 00:00:21,790
But you're in Class 3, so we'll 
have PE and stuff together.

4
00:00:21,790 --> 00:00:23,660
Hey, Hananoi!

5
00:00:24,080 --> 00:00:26,380
We're in the same class again.

6
00:00:26,380 --> 00:00:27,460
Let's have a great year!

7
00:00:29,090 --> 00:00:31,420
I'm in Class 3 too.

8
00:00:31,420 --> 00:00:34,930
We've been in the same class forever, 
Hotaru. Makes me wanna barf!

9
00:00:34,930 --> 00:00:36,800
Even Shibamu is in Class 4.

10
00:00:36,800 --> 00:00:40,680
But you'll have Keigo-kun with you.
I'm sure you'll be fine.

11
00:00:41,310 --> 00:00:42,930
You've got me, right?

12
00:00:42,930 --> 00:00:45,730
You're in a totally different world
 from us girls.

13
00:00:47,230 --> 00:00:48,330
Wh-What is it?

14
00:00:49,360 --> 00:00:53,070
Hotaru-chan, you always call that 
guy by his first name, right?

15
00:00:53,360 --> 00:00:54,530
"That guy"?

16
00:00:55,070 --> 00:00:56,950
Oh, you mean Keigo-kun?

17
00:00:57,870 --> 00:01:02,120
Isn't it about time you start 
using my first name too?

18
00:01:04,120 --> 00:01:06,420
U-Um, did you just say something?

19
00:01:06,420 --> 00:01:08,380
No, it was nothing.

20
00:01:09,380 --> 00:01:11,710
Okay, I'll see you on the way home.

21
00:01:16,300 --> 00:01:18,470
First names, huh...?

22
00:01:21,470 --> 00:01:24,220
<i>April is the season of change.</i>

23
00:02:55,610 --> 00:03:01,950
Episode 10

24
00:02:55,610 --> 00:03:01,950
Our First Second Year

25
00:02:56,940 --> 00:02:58,820
Yo, Hananoi!

26
00:02:58,820 --> 00:03:01,030
Find anyone to celebrate your birthday with?

27
00:03:01,820 --> 00:03:02,740
Whoa!

28
00:03:03,620 --> 00:03:05,780
Oh, come on, Kei-chan!

29
00:03:05,780 --> 00:03:06,910
Asami-san.

30
00:03:06,910 --> 00:03:07,870
Yes?!

31
00:03:07,870 --> 00:03:11,870
When did you start calling 
this guy by his first name?

32
00:03:11,870 --> 00:03:16,050
When? I think it was right 
after we first met.

33
00:03:17,460 --> 00:03:20,170
So it was important to start early...

34
00:03:22,890 --> 00:03:24,720
Shibamu, good morning!

35
00:03:24,720 --> 00:03:25,970
Good morning!

36
00:03:25,970 --> 00:03:28,100
Let's have a great second year together.

37
00:03:28,100 --> 00:03:31,520
All right. Please take your seats, everyone.

38
00:03:33,270 --> 00:03:35,060
<i>A new classroom.</i>

39
00:03:35,730 --> 00:03:37,830
<i>New classmates.</i>

40
00:03:41,150 --> 00:03:43,320
<i>A new normal...</i>

41
00:03:45,240 --> 00:03:48,040
Who is that upperclassman?! He's so cool!

42
00:03:48,330 --> 00:03:50,290
<i>...is already unfolding.</i>

43
00:03:49,290 --> 00:03:51,080
I wonder what grade he's in.

44
00:03:51,080 --> 00:03:53,830
The Next Day

45
00:03:54,500 --> 00:03:58,590
Hibiki

46
00:03:54,500 --> 00:03:58,590
Thanks!

47
00:03:54,500 --> 00:03:58,590
Let's eat lunch together!

48
00:03:54,500 --> 00:03:58,590
Hibiki

49
00:03:54,500 --> 00:03:58,590
Sorry!
I want to get used to
my new class, so I'm
going to eat lunch
with the girls here
for a while

50
00:03:54,500 --> 00:03:58,590
Beg Ya Pardon

51
00:03:58,590 --> 00:03:59,710
What?!

52
00:04:00,210 --> 00:04:02,510
Oh well. It figures.

53
00:04:02,510 --> 00:04:07,890
Yeah. But what should I do?
 I'm supposed to eat with Hananoi-kun today.

54
00:04:07,890 --> 00:04:09,260
Don't sweat it.

55
00:04:09,260 --> 00:04:10,220
Hotaru-chan!

56
00:04:10,980 --> 00:04:12,480
Let's have lunch together.

57
00:04:12,480 --> 00:04:14,900
Wow!

58
00:04:14,900 --> 00:04:16,980
Hananoi-kun, perfect timing!

59
00:04:18,150 --> 00:04:19,730
I see.

60
00:04:20,110 --> 00:04:22,610
You don't need to worry about me.

61
00:04:22,610 --> 00:04:25,740
But I don't want to leave you alone, Shibamu.

62
00:04:25,740 --> 00:04:26,990
Wow!

63
00:04:26,570 --> 00:04:27,870
What are they talking about?

64
00:04:27,450 --> 00:04:29,030
He's so cool!

65
00:04:28,530 --> 00:04:32,540
Well, worst case, I eat by myself.
That doesn't bother me at all.

66
00:04:33,370 --> 00:04:40,630
Boyfriend

67
00:04:33,370 --> 00:04:40,630
Friends

68
00:04:33,710 --> 00:04:36,920
<i>Who do I put first
in a situation like this?</i>

69
00:04:36,920 --> 00:04:40,090
<i>It would be best if the three
 of us could eat together!</i>

70
00:04:40,630 --> 00:04:43,580
<i>But I doubt Hananoi-kun would go for that...</i>

71
00:04:46,300 --> 00:04:49,810
Shibamura-san, 
why don't you just eat with us?

72
00:04:49,810 --> 00:04:52,770
Huh? D-Do you mean it?

73
00:04:55,600 --> 00:04:59,440
Um, but it won't be just for today.

74
00:05:00,150 --> 00:05:01,610
That's okay.

75
00:05:01,610 --> 00:05:03,900
I've decided I can live with it.

76
00:05:04,360 --> 00:05:05,740
Oh...

77
00:05:06,410 --> 00:05:09,790
Okay, then let's find some other time 
for just the two of us later on!

78
00:05:11,660 --> 00:05:12,540
Sure.

79
00:05:14,250 --> 00:05:19,250
Oh! I forgot to get a drink! 
Sorry, I'll be right back!

80
00:05:25,840 --> 00:05:30,600
Listen, I'm really sorry to impose like this.

81
00:05:30,600 --> 00:05:31,720
It's fine.

82
00:05:33,680 --> 00:05:39,930
Um, Hananoi-san, what do you do for lunch 
when you don't eat with Hotaru-chan?

83
00:05:40,980 --> 00:05:43,230
I find somewhere to eat alone.

84
00:05:43,230 --> 00:05:46,570
Ah. Eating alone is easiest, isn't it?

85
00:05:47,240 --> 00:05:49,160
But I guess everyone else hates it.

86
00:05:49,740 --> 00:05:53,190
<i>You really didn't need 
to make a fuss about me, Hotaru.</i>

87
00:05:54,540 --> 00:05:56,580
Yeah, I guess it is easier.

88
00:05:57,670 --> 00:06:00,380
Though I like eating with Hotaru-chan more.

89
00:06:01,040 --> 00:06:02,500
What about you, Shibamura-san?

90
00:06:03,460 --> 00:06:06,590
Well, I guess the same goes for me.

91
00:06:09,050 --> 00:06:13,140
Then you don't have to 
feel so bad about this.

92
00:06:15,100 --> 00:06:18,310
Hey, you two! Thanks for waiting!

93
00:06:19,610 --> 00:06:20,820
Chow time!

94
00:06:21,480 --> 00:06:23,070
Hamburg steak!

95
00:06:23,070 --> 00:06:26,190
But I really should save 
the main dish for last!

96
00:06:27,440 --> 00:06:28,900
Yum!

97
00:06:30,910 --> 00:06:32,830
Ah, this is so fun.

98
00:06:32,830 --> 00:06:34,650
It really is, isn't it?

99
00:06:34,650 --> 00:06:37,410
<i>Th-They agree on something?</i>

100
00:06:40,580 --> 00:06:43,290
Okay, should we start heading back?

101
00:06:43,290 --> 00:06:46,010
Sorry, but we need a minute.

102
00:06:46,010 --> 00:06:47,700
Why don't you go on, Shibamura-san?

103
00:06:48,320 --> 00:06:50,130
Sure. Take your time.

104
00:06:53,100 --> 00:06:54,430
What's up?

105
00:07:00,930 --> 00:07:01,890
I'm thinking...

106
00:07:02,810 --> 00:07:05,960
I won't get a chance 
to hold you like this for a while.

107
00:07:06,690 --> 00:07:07,900
I'm recharging.

108
00:07:07,900 --> 00:07:09,780
I-I see.

109
00:07:14,200 --> 00:07:18,910
Oh, right! Um, was lunch today okay with you?

110
00:07:19,370 --> 00:07:21,870
If you really didn't like it, please tell me.

111
00:07:23,250 --> 00:07:25,410
You don't need to worry about that.

112
00:07:26,750 --> 00:07:32,920
I'm sure that past me would've
 hated a situation like today's.

113
00:07:33,330 --> 00:07:39,550
But I can tell that you really 
care about me. It shows.

114
00:07:41,600 --> 00:07:45,560
So I'm just getting my fill of you
to last me for a while.

115
00:07:49,900 --> 00:07:52,070
I guess we should go back.

116
00:07:52,740 --> 00:07:53,700
Huh?

117
00:07:58,120 --> 00:08:02,670
Sorry. I need another ten seconds after all.

118
00:08:08,590 --> 00:08:11,090
S-So, what did you think of lunch?

119
00:08:11,090 --> 00:08:12,840
I thought it was pretty fun.

120
00:08:13,430 --> 00:08:16,430
That's the most I've ever talked
with Hananoi-san.

121
00:08:17,760 --> 00:08:23,100
He said that he likes eating with you
 more than eating alone.

122
00:08:23,100 --> 00:08:24,940
That really stuck with me.

123
00:08:25,730 --> 00:08:29,150
Seems like you two are 
really hitting it off. I'm glad.

124
00:08:30,690 --> 00:08:36,740
<i>I'm sure that past me would've
 hated a situation like today's.</i>

125
00:08:39,450 --> 00:08:43,500
<i>I wonder if I can talk to him about it now.</i>

126
00:08:44,290 --> 00:08:49,670
<i>It's something I've been thinking about
but haven't had courage to bring up.</i>

127
00:08:50,460 --> 00:08:53,720
<i>Friends, huh? I don't think I need any.</i>

128
00:08:54,380 --> 00:08:59,680
<i>It seems like Hananoi-kun cares
 a lot about his alone time.</i>

129
00:08:59,680 --> 00:09:02,890
<i>So this never felt like something 
I should push him on.</i>

130
00:09:03,430 --> 00:09:07,150
<i>But things might not always be that way.</i>

131
00:09:08,480 --> 00:09:11,360
<i>It's like something, bit by bit,</i>

132
00:09:13,740 --> 00:09:15,400
<i>is changing inside him.</i>

133
00:09:17,530 --> 00:09:19,780
I can't take it anymore!

134
00:09:19,780 --> 00:09:24,500
I've tried my hardest for two weeks,
but enough is enough!

135
00:09:24,500 --> 00:09:27,290
As long as we get along, 
we'll be friends eventually!

136
00:09:27,290 --> 00:09:30,250
I'm so glad we're all eating together again!

137
00:09:30,250 --> 00:09:33,300
Things are more exciting with Hibiki around.

138
00:09:33,300 --> 00:09:36,800
Yeah, but you know,
now that I'm in class with Hananoi-kun,

139
00:09:36,800 --> 00:09:40,260
it's so obvious how he goes
 out of his way to be alone.

140
00:09:41,260 --> 00:09:46,810
When I saw how he keeps to himself,
I kind of threw my hands up.

141
00:09:46,810 --> 00:09:51,150
Um, actually, I wanted to ask 
you two for advice about that.

142
00:09:53,110 --> 00:09:54,360
Oh, yeah?

143
00:09:54,820 --> 00:09:58,450
Things are back to normal, huh?
 You must be happy.

144
00:09:58,450 --> 00:09:59,410
Yeah.

145
00:10:00,160 --> 00:10:03,830
S-So after this, I mean from now on,

146
00:10:05,160 --> 00:10:09,660
if it's okay with you, will you eat 
 lunch with us, Hananoi-kun?

147
00:10:11,250 --> 00:10:13,670
Um, but that sounds...

148
00:10:14,000 --> 00:10:18,340
Oh! We can still have days 
when it's just the two of us.

149
00:10:18,340 --> 00:10:20,050
I mean the rest of the week.

150
00:10:20,300 --> 00:10:24,470
If you'd rather eat alone,
we can just keep things the way they were.

151
00:10:24,470 --> 00:10:28,310
But these past two weeks, you've been 
talking like normal with Shibamu,

152
00:10:28,310 --> 00:10:32,860
so as long as it would be 
okay with you...

153
00:10:36,400 --> 00:10:40,410
If anything, I wonder, would it be okay with you?

154
00:10:40,410 --> 00:10:42,700
You've finally got some girl time together.

155
00:10:42,700 --> 00:10:44,410
I don't mind at all!

156
00:10:45,580 --> 00:10:49,500
But I'm sorry. I don't exactly know
 how things are going to go.

157
00:10:49,870 --> 00:10:53,840
I think it would be fun to hang out together,

158
00:10:53,840 --> 00:10:57,590
but there's a chance it may not go over well.

159
00:10:57,970 --> 00:10:58,920
But still...

160
00:11:02,140 --> 00:11:06,560
<i>I want to try it, and then we can decide 
what's the most fun for us, Hananoi-kun!</i>

161
00:11:12,350 --> 00:11:15,270
All right. I'll think about it.

162
00:11:18,400 --> 00:11:19,450
Okay!

163
00:11:20,070 --> 00:11:25,870
<i>Trying something new can be 
scary and confusing at times,</i>

164
00:11:26,580 --> 00:11:31,000
<i>but if it can make
the people I care about happy,</i>

165
00:11:31,420 --> 00:11:33,040
<i>I want to do my part.</i>

166
00:11:34,340 --> 00:11:39,090
<i>Yeah. Change isn't always a bad thing.</i>

167
00:11:39,090 --> 00:11:41,680
<i>Hananoi-kun is the one who taught me that.</i>

168
00:11:45,350 --> 00:11:48,850
It's so warm today! 
Eating outside was the right move.

169
00:11:48,850 --> 00:11:52,940
Strawberry Milk

170
00:11:49,350 --> 00:11:51,600
But man, Hananoi, is that all you got?

171
00:11:51,600 --> 00:11:54,060
All right, all right. Want some of mine?

172
00:11:54,060 --> 00:11:55,180
No way.

173
00:11:55,180 --> 00:11:59,150
Then how about mine? I made extra today.

174
00:11:59,400 --> 00:12:01,240
Wow, that looks so good!

175
00:12:01,240 --> 00:12:02,780
You guys too, if you want.

176
00:12:02,780 --> 00:12:06,410
Huh. It's unusual for you to cook.

177
00:12:06,780 --> 00:12:11,540
Well, to tell you the truth,
I was practicing cooking for Saki-kun,

178
00:12:11,540 --> 00:12:15,460
but since it was just practice, 
my mom did most of the work.

179
00:12:15,460 --> 00:12:17,670
Hmm? Who the heck is Saki?

180
00:12:25,620 --> 00:12:27,390
No way... What?!

181
00:12:27,390 --> 00:12:30,180
Hey, what's Hananoi's first name again?

182
00:12:30,770 --> 00:12:32,980
Would you shut up a minute?

183
00:12:33,320 --> 00:12:38,610
<i>Yeah, I knew that would 
embarrass him! I'm so sorry!</i>

184
00:12:39,980 --> 00:12:44,570
<i>It was the day Hotaru had to go
 to the vet for surgery...</i>

185
00:12:48,620 --> 00:12:52,830
U-Um, is that you over there, Yao-kun?

186
00:12:54,420 --> 00:12:57,880
Wh-What's wrong?! Are you okay?
 Should I get someone?

187
00:12:57,330 --> 00:12:58,710
Don't tell anyone!

188
00:12:58,710 --> 00:13:00,300
O-Okay.

189
00:13:00,880 --> 00:13:03,840
Sohei-kun! Where are you?

190
00:13:04,840 --> 00:13:06,010
Non-chan!

191
00:13:06,010 --> 00:13:07,390
Hotaru-chan.

192
00:13:07,850 --> 00:13:08,850
<i>Hotaru?</i>

193
00:13:08,850 --> 00:13:10,380
Have you seen Sohei-kun?

194
00:13:10,380 --> 00:13:13,270
I-I don't think he's over here.

195
00:13:13,270 --> 00:13:16,480
Okay. Sohei-kun!

196
00:13:19,690 --> 00:13:22,320
Everyone's looking for you, Yao-kun.

197
00:13:22,320 --> 00:13:26,030
It might be better to hide 
somewhere farther away.

198
00:13:26,490 --> 00:13:28,150
Well, I'd better go.

199
00:13:31,160 --> 00:13:33,000
Wait, Hotaru!

200
00:13:35,250 --> 00:13:38,540
<i>That was how I became friends with Hotako.</i>

201
00:13:39,540 --> 00:13:42,460
<i>She shared the name
 of a precious family member.</i>

202
00:13:43,260 --> 00:13:44,550
<i>She was kind.</i>

203
00:13:45,260 --> 00:13:47,300
<i>And she was always true to herself.</i>

204
00:13:47,960 --> 00:13:50,970
<i>Whenever I was with her, I felt so relaxed.</i>

205
00:13:51,640 --> 00:13:55,480
<i>She's the kind of person 
you just want to see happy.</i>

206
00:14:03,690 --> 00:14:07,150
<i>Someday, somewhere...</i>

207
00:14:11,490 --> 00:14:12,530
<i>I hope you find someone</i>

208
00:14:13,790 --> 00:14:15,120
<i>who makes you happy.</i>

209
00:14:17,160 --> 00:14:20,170
Otowa South Elementary

210
00:14:17,160 --> 00:14:20,170
Hananoi (sixth grade, class 5)

211
00:14:17,160 --> 00:14:20,170
Now dating

212
00:14:17,160 --> 00:14:20,170
Hotako (sixth grade, class 1)

213
00:14:17,160 --> 00:14:20,170
Me

214
00:14:17,160 --> 00:14:20,170
Classmates

215
00:14:17,160 --> 00:14:20,170
Does she know Hananoi went to our school?

216
00:14:19,120 --> 00:14:20,170
Hmm...

217
00:14:24,050 --> 00:14:25,420
Yao!

218
00:14:25,840 --> 00:14:27,680
Wanna come to karaoke with everybody?

219
00:14:28,010 --> 00:14:30,680
Sorry, I have work today.

220
00:14:34,010 --> 00:14:39,900
U-Um, ever since you found that book 
for me, I couldn't get you off my mind.

221
00:14:40,690 --> 00:14:42,150
No thanks.

222
00:14:42,150 --> 00:14:43,940
I have no interest in you whatsoever.

223
00:14:43,940 --> 00:14:46,400
<i>Man, he sure doesn't pull any punches.</i>

224
00:14:47,740 --> 00:14:48,530
Oh...

225
00:14:49,320 --> 00:14:52,950
Sorry. I didn't mean to spy on you.

226
00:14:54,540 --> 00:14:58,000
Do you get asked out a lot by random girls?

227
00:14:58,460 --> 00:14:59,250
Huh?

228
00:14:59,710 --> 00:15:01,260
Is that any of your business?

229
00:15:01,830 --> 00:15:06,340
Well, no. I was just thinking how 
tough that must be for Hinase.

230
00:15:06,760 --> 00:15:10,760
She used to be so easygoing 
in elementary school.

231
00:15:10,760 --> 00:15:12,760
I guess I just worry about her.

232
00:15:13,680 --> 00:15:19,100
Oh, speaking of which, didn't you 
guys know each other before too?

233
00:15:21,190 --> 00:15:24,480
The other day, when I was 
flipping through my yearbook,

234
00:15:24,480 --> 00:15:26,650
I saw a guy with your name in class 5.

235
00:15:27,150 --> 00:15:31,410
Then I remembered we had a 
transfer student in sixth grade.

236
00:15:32,870 --> 00:15:37,160
Why didn't you say anything?
 Hinase doesn't realize it either, does she?

237
00:15:38,290 --> 00:15:41,750
I don't see any point in telling her 
if she doesn't remember.

238
00:15:42,290 --> 00:15:45,630
I don't particularly care 
for who I was back then.

239
00:15:46,210 --> 00:15:47,920
Oh... okay.

240
00:15:48,710 --> 00:15:51,300
But still, isn't that something you should...

241
00:15:53,920 --> 00:15:56,640
If you want to tell her, go ahead.

242
00:16:00,100 --> 00:16:03,190
<i>Yeah, I really can't figure him out.</i>

243
00:16:03,810 --> 00:16:07,320
<i>He seems to put up a wall
 with everyone, but...</i>

244
00:16:07,320 --> 00:16:08,900
Oh? What's that?

245
00:16:11,320 --> 00:16:13,820
It was a birthday gift from Hinase-san.

246
00:16:16,280 --> 00:16:19,700
<i>Maybe he isn't such a bad guy after all.</i>

247
00:16:20,000 --> 00:16:24,210
<i>Should I just drop it and not do anything?</i>

248
00:16:26,000 --> 00:16:27,290
<i>Hananoi?</i>

249
00:16:27,840 --> 00:16:30,710
<i>Oh, yeah! The transfer kid who wore glasses?</i>

250
00:16:30,960 --> 00:16:35,960
You ever hear anything about him being 
friends with that Hinase girl from my class?

251
00:16:35,960 --> 00:16:39,980
<i>You mean Hotako-chan?
The nerdy girl you went out with?</i>

252
00:16:39,980 --> 00:16:41,140
Huh?!

253
00:16:41,140 --> 00:16:45,600
<i>People were spreading rumors, man. 
Someone said they saw you two alone.</i>

254
00:16:45,600 --> 00:16:48,270
We were only talking about my dog!

255
00:16:47,650 --> 00:16:50,730
<i>Yeah, well, you were at least friends, right?</i>

256
00:16:50,730 --> 00:16:52,700
Who knows?

257
00:16:53,240 --> 00:16:57,620
She told me she didn't 
think we were <i>that</i> close.

258
00:16:58,030 --> 00:17:04,290
And now we talk all the time, 
but whenever I get close, she backs off.

259
00:17:04,290 --> 00:17:11,380
She acts kinda cold, you know? 
Maybe she hates me. I don't get it.

260
00:17:11,380 --> 00:17:13,920
<i>Wow, I never hear you 
complain like this, Sohei.</i>

261
00:17:13,920 --> 00:17:14,800
Oh.

262
00:17:19,050 --> 00:17:21,180
<i>Was I complaining?</i>

263
00:17:23,980 --> 00:17:26,400
<i>What the hell am I doing?</i>

264
00:17:27,480 --> 00:17:31,190
Hotako. Hotako!

265
00:17:32,530 --> 00:17:36,190
Yao-kun, why do you always call me Hotako?

266
00:17:36,190 --> 00:17:39,990
Don't you wanna call your friends 
by their name or nickname?

267
00:17:40,780 --> 00:17:43,160
F-Friends?

268
00:17:44,160 --> 00:17:45,830
I guess we are friends!

269
00:17:48,000 --> 00:17:50,290
Thank you very much for calling.

270
00:17:50,840 --> 00:17:54,050
Yes. A picture book with animals?

271
00:17:54,970 --> 00:17:59,470
<i>Hmm. Animals, animals...</i>

272
00:18:03,970 --> 00:18:08,600
Yao-kun? Are you okay? Is something wrong?

273
00:18:09,560 --> 00:18:11,690
<i>What?! What happened?</i>

274
00:18:14,280 --> 00:18:16,860
Sorry, I know I'm at work.

275
00:18:16,860 --> 00:18:19,660
Wh-Why don't you go in the back for now?

276
00:18:19,660 --> 00:18:22,490
No, I'm good! I'll be fine.

277
00:18:22,490 --> 00:18:24,620
Ah! There you are, Yao!

278
00:18:25,330 --> 00:18:28,080
I was in the neighborhood, 
so I thought I'd stop by.

279
00:18:28,670 --> 00:18:31,880
I'm sorry, but that's not Yao-kun!

280
00:18:31,880 --> 00:18:33,930
Huh? That's totally Yao.

281
00:18:33,930 --> 00:18:38,010
I'm very sorry! Would you mind 
seeing him some other time?

282
00:18:38,010 --> 00:18:41,680
What's this about?
 Who are you to him anyway?

283
00:18:42,140 --> 00:18:44,190
I-I'm his friend!

284
00:18:46,060 --> 00:18:48,770
Well, I'm his friend too!

285
00:18:52,230 --> 00:18:54,300
I'm working right now.

286
00:18:57,320 --> 00:18:58,450
Sorry, okay?

287
00:19:02,450 --> 00:19:04,870
Well? Are you better now?

288
00:19:04,870 --> 00:19:06,960
Uh, yeah.

289
00:19:09,210 --> 00:19:11,920
Hotako, I'm real sorry about before.

290
00:19:11,920 --> 00:19:14,290
No, I shouldn't have done that.

291
00:19:17,380 --> 00:19:18,630
That name...

292
00:19:18,630 --> 00:19:19,170
Huh?

293
00:19:19,630 --> 00:19:22,100
You've gone back to calling me Hotako.

294
00:19:22,410 --> 00:19:24,050
Oh, sorry!

295
00:19:24,050 --> 00:19:29,520
No, it's okay! I think I've started 
to understand how you feel.

296
00:19:31,810 --> 00:19:35,650
It's hard to change what 
you've always called someone.

297
00:19:36,150 --> 00:19:40,870
It feels really weird and makes 
you so nervous every time.

298
00:19:43,120 --> 00:19:47,410
When he said I could take my time,
 it was such a relief.

299
00:19:47,860 --> 00:19:53,000
So... do you mean I can 
keep calling you Hotako?

300
00:19:53,460 --> 00:19:57,170
I guess I mean to make the switch
when it feels right to you.

301
00:19:58,800 --> 00:20:01,550
Okay. That's a relief.

302
00:20:03,050 --> 00:20:05,300
You sure never change, Yao-kun.

303
00:20:05,300 --> 00:20:06,060
Huh?

304
00:20:07,310 --> 00:20:11,140
You've always been sentimental about dogs.

305
00:20:11,140 --> 00:20:13,690
Well, you don't change either, Hotako!

306
00:20:13,690 --> 00:20:15,690
You've always been a terrible liar.

307
00:20:15,690 --> 00:20:17,020
Huh?

308
00:20:17,320 --> 00:20:19,400
<i>Oh... This feeling.</i>

309
00:20:20,360 --> 00:20:24,570
<i>It's been so long. 
It feels like I'm floating.</i>

310
00:20:25,490 --> 00:20:28,160
<i>When we laugh together,
it's like a weight off my shoulders.</i>

311
00:20:28,990 --> 00:20:33,920
<i>I used to really love those moments.</i>

312
00:20:40,550 --> 00:20:44,430
Um, listen. I don't mean 
anything weird by this, but...

313
00:20:45,720 --> 00:20:49,170
Hotako, do you like me? Or dislike me?

314
00:20:51,180 --> 00:20:52,230
Uh...

315
00:20:55,850 --> 00:20:56,900
I...

316
00:20:57,980 --> 00:21:00,070
I respect you!

317
00:21:00,440 --> 00:21:02,780
R-Respect?

318
00:21:02,780 --> 00:21:05,950
Yeah! Since before. I always have!

319
00:21:06,620 --> 00:21:11,370
Really? You respect me, huh?

320
00:21:11,910 --> 00:21:13,910
That's sort of flattering.

321
00:21:15,790 --> 00:21:17,920
<i>Why do I feel like this?</i>

322
00:21:19,340 --> 00:21:24,130
Hey, you said you wanted to find a way
 to thank me after you guys came over to my house.

323
00:21:24,130 --> 00:21:25,800
Yeah, I did.

324
00:21:25,800 --> 00:21:28,850
Listen, Hotako...

325
00:21:30,910 --> 00:21:32,960
I want to talk to you a lot more.

326
00:21:39,000 --> 00:21:43,240
So, I was thinking, why don't 
we all go somewhere again?

327
00:21:43,630 --> 00:21:44,400
Huh?

328
00:23:17,300 --> 00:23:18,820
A get-together?

329
00:23:18,820 --> 00:23:19,690
Yeah.

330
00:23:20,110 --> 00:23:23,670
I'm not trying to get you 
to like me or nanything.

331
00:23:23,670 --> 00:23:26,340
but can't we just talk like normal people?

332
00:23:26,340 --> 00:23:29,840
I mean, she's probably worried about us too.

333
00:23:30,370 --> 00:23:33,760
Do you really wanna keep putting 
your girlfriend through that?

